ccglue
------------------------------------------
ccglue is intended to be the interfacing app between cscope and ctags. It can
generate cross-reference tag files that can be interfaced with the Vim CCTree
plugin

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20261107-1
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.13-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://ccglue.sourceforge.net/

Canonical download:
  mirror://sourceforge/ccglue/ccglue-release-0.6.0.tar.bz2

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack ccglue-0.6.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./ccglue-0.6.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/ccglue-0.6.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/ccglue-0.6.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(ccglue)
  /usr/bin/ccglue.exe
